    "reasoning": "q-18621: The x^{22} term uses eleven factors of x^2, giving coefficient \\binom{13}{11}3^2=78\\cdot9=702. q-135896: The binomial expansion is 256-256x+96x^2-16x^3+x^4, matching the selected initial terms. Both answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. The current source correctly represents binomial coefficients using parenthesized, zero-bar \\genfrac expressions; the earlier claim of authored fraction-notation errors does not apply to this authoritative evidence.",
